OL,3,GNEWSACould experts have a solution to
OL,4,Atoxic algae?
OL,5,
OL,6,FExperts are testing out a new method
OL,7,Fthat could see a way to tackle
OL,8,Fblue-green algae blooms.
OL,10,FThe toxic algae is actually
OL,11,Fcyanobacteria rather than a true algae
OL,12,Fand can increase dramatically in heat,
OL,13,Fmaking people and animals sick when
OL,14,Fingested.
OL,16,FDr Sanjay Nagarajan, from the Institute
OL,17,Ffor Sustainability and Climate Change
OL,18,Fat the University of Bath, took his
OL,19,Fchild to the Warminster Pleasure
OL,20,FGrounds in Wiltshire when he saw the
OL,21,Flake there closed because of the bloom.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,349,340,200,160,0,100
